{title: We Gather Together}
{artist: Dutch hymn · tr. Theodore Baker}
{key: F}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 84}

Verse 1
We [F]gather to[Bb]gether to [C]ask the Lord's [F]blessing —
he [Dm]chastens and [G]hastens his [C]will to make known;
the [F]wicked op[Bb]pressing now [C]cease from dis[Dm]tressing:
sing [F]praises to [C]his name, he for[F]gets not his [C]own.

Verse 2
Beside [F]us to guide [C]us, our God [F]with us
joining, [Dm]Ordaining, maintaining [G]His kingdom [C]divine; So from the
beginning [F]the fight we [C]were winning; Thou,
Lord, [F]were at [C]our side, all forgets glory be [C]Thine!

Verse 3
We [F]all do extol [C]Thee, Thou Leader [F]triumphant, And
pray [Dm]that Thou [G]still [C]our Defender will be.
Let [F]Thy congregation escape [C]tribulation; Thy Name
be [F]ever praised! [C]O forgets Lord, make us [C]free!
